A2b-recession.statement:
\label{A2b-recession}
There are constants $B_i<\infty$, depending only on the marked $Y$ and
the chosen tangent coordinates, such that every embedded pointed disc
avoiding the other marked points has conformal radius at most $B_i$.
For a canonical cap one has
\begin{equation}\label{A2b-collar-bound}
 r_i(s)\leq B_i\exp\left(
   -\frac{\arctan(\operatorname{csch}(\pi\sqrt{s_i}))}{\sqrt{s_i}}
                         \right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, for every $s_0>0$ and $p\geq0$,
\begin{equation}\label{A2b-recession-formula}
 \lim_{t\to\infty}\frac{S(s_0+tp)-S(s_0)}t=K(p).
\end{equation}

A6-graphic.statement:
\label{A6-graphic}
For the framed logarithmic realization above, every $G_K$-compatible outer isomorphism
$\Delta_{Y,N}\simeq\Delta_{Y',N'}$ preserves the entire semi-graph of anabelioids: vertices, nodes, cusps, and incidence.

A7-real-topology.statement:
\label{A7-real-topology}
The real locus and the first Galois cohomology group are
\[
 \begin{array}{c|c|c}
 E & E(\R) & H^1(\R,E)\\\hline
 E_a & (\R/\Z)\times(\Z/2\Z) & \Z/2\Z\\
 E'_a & \R/\Z & 0.
 \end{array}
\]
The quotients of the complex curves by their standard real structures are respectively an annulus and a M\"obius band. The unique nontrivial $E_a$-torsor has no real point; its antiholomorphic involution is $[z]\mapsto[\bar{z}+1/2]$, and its quotient is a Klein bottle. These torsors together with the two pointed families classify all smooth projective geometrically connected genus-one curves over $\R$.

C-functor-counter.statement:
\label{C-functor-counter}
The formal exponential need not be injective, and neither exponential
map need be surjective, for arbitrary module functors.
